.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The LIVE evidence pool is TRACKED, deliberately. check_provenance.py matches every numeric
# claim in README.md and EXPLAINER.md against a script's captured stdout, and without this
# directory a reader who clones has to re-run all sixteen scripts (about three hours, and
# permutation_design.py alone is nearly five) before the guard can tell them anything. A claim
# that can only be checked by people who already have the cache is not checkable.
#
# This is NOT a contradiction of the STATUS.json rule below, and the difference is the reason
# both rules can coexist: STATUS.json describes MUTABLE CURRENT STATE and is stale the moment
# a commit lands. The provenance cache is a RECORD OF WHAT A SPECIFIC VERSION OF A SCRIPT
# PRINTED, keyed by a SHA-256 of that script's source (see meta.json). Change the registered
# script and the key changes and the entry stops matching, automatically.
#
# WHAT THAT HASH DOES NOT COVER, stated because the README used to overstate it: the entry
# file only, never the modules it imports. Before the 2026-08-26 split those were the same
# thing. They are not any more, so an edit inside an imported module leaves the key intact and
# the entry reports as cached when it is stale. Verified by changing a within-subject count
# from 41 to 39 inside a split module and watching the check pass it.
#
# Contents are VERBATIM stdout and are never edited, including the three files that carry a
# local MNE download path (~/mne_data/...). Scrubbing them would make the cache no longer a
# faithful capture, which is the property the whole guard rests on.
#
# The dated backup pools beside it stay ignored: they are superseded evidence, and a stale
# pool that check_provenance.py could read by mistake is worse than no pool. This rule is
# written as `.provenance_cache.*/` rather than the old `.provenance_cache*/` on purpose --
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so a `!` negation after
# the wider glob would have silently done nothing.
.provenance_cache.*/

# permutation_design.py block checkpoints: raw per-replicate scores, regenerable.
.permutation_design_cache/

# Derived state -- regenerate with status.py. Never commit; that is how state becomes stale history.
STATUS.json

# Local working records and ops tooling, deliberately outside the public tree. The
# process records stay on disk for provenance; status.py writes STATUS.json for the
# vault and measures the repo, not the EEG data.
status.py
CLAUDE.md
docs/process/
